+## Current amendment — PDR-1.11 / Map Share Privacy V1 · 2026-10-29
+
+Source/decisor for DR-133: the current direct [Founder request r2](../audits/growth-layer-2026-10-29/FOUNDER_REQUEST_R2.md) of 2026-10-29. **DECIDED / CURRENT_PRODUCT_DECISION.** It resolves the conflict recorded as GRW-04 and replaces PDR-1.10's earlier reading that a background map was not authorized; that reading was never applied. The Founder named Strava's sharing and Map Visibility controls and Runna's user-initiated external share as protection benchmarks, not templates or Product Truth. Training/Safety/Privacy authority prevails over Growth. Record: [GRW record](../audits/growth-layer-2026-10-29/RECORD.md).
+
+| ID | Current decision / rationale | Scope, supersession, dependents |
+|---|---|---|
+| DR-133 | **Real maps are allowed in external shareables of GPS activities in V1, under this policy:** (1) map sharing is always explicitly started by the person; (2) the first 200 m and the last 200 m of the route are hidden by default in the artifact; (3) the person can change that protection for an individual activity before sharing; (4) the route/map can be hidden completely; (5) at least four options: **Map** (real map + protected route), **Route** (route trace, no map), **Photo/Overlay**, and share **without route**; (6) the exact final artifact is previewed before any external share; (7) the interface discreetly shows that start and end are protected and lets the person edit it; (8) raw GPS geometry never goes into the image/social sharing mechanism: **raw GPS → privacy filtering → share-safe geometry → map/artifact rendering → external share**, so protection happens before the external artifact exists; (9) sharing a map neither changes nor removes the private activity's full data; (10) no automatic sharing. Persistent **Privacy Zones** (Home, Work, custom location) are a planned evolution with no infrastructure now; Security and Product/UX evaluate them before they materialize, because they handle precise location. **Not authorized:** public feed, social map, real-time location, residence exposure, social graph, Crew, automatic sharing, raw GPS export. | **Supersedes, for external shareables only:** DR-91's "linha abstrata sem mapa de fundo" and its fixed start/end cut; UXS SHR-09's fixed 500 m cut and its "sem mapa de fundo, ruas, nomes de lugar"; PA §7's "Rota entra só como traçado abstrato aparado"; the designer context's route sentence. It also qualifies the location exclusions in the PDM Shareability row, EM §6 and CF F10 step 2/S12, for the protected map or route the person chooses only. **Unchanged:** completed activities only, never live; the route/map is off whenever the preview opens; "Rotas no app" stays its own purpose, off by default, separate from the GPS-recording permission (SHR-09, DR-109); a minimum visible route after protection (SHR-09) until Product/UX + Security revise it; the static preview warning that a route's shape can reveal where the person runs or lives; place names, addresses, coordinates, absolute altitude and times stay excluded as fields, titles, alt-text, file names and metadata (SHR-06, SHR-10); on-device composition with only pixels leaving the device; images re-encoded without EXIF/GPS; the minimal projection record (G07). L014 is satisfied by explicit initiation, exact preview and default protection; it is not edited. **The map provider** that renders the share-safe area is a recipient to declare (DR-109, G07); none is chosen here. **Before implementation** Security re-verifies the boundary under this policy (DR-91 had SECURITY_READY_WITH_CONDITIONS for the abstract trace), Product/UX + Security set the open details below, and copy/legal text is G07. |
+
+**Confirmed state:**
+
+| Item | State |
+|---|---|
+| MAP_BACKGROUND_IN_EXTERNAL_SHARE_V1 | ALLOWED under DR-133 |
+| SHARE_ROUTE_OPTIONS | Map (real map + protected route) · Route (trace, no map) · Photo/Overlay · no route |
+| START_END_PROTECTION_DEFAULT | first 200 m and last 200 m hidden; editable per activity before sharing |
+| RAW_GPS_IN_SHARE_MECHANISM | NEVER; share-safe geometry only, protection before rendering |
+| AUTOMATIC_SHARING | NO |
+| PRIVATE_ACTIVITY_DATA_ON_SHARE | UNCHANGED (sharing never edits or trims it) |
+| PRIVACY_ZONES | PLANNED; no infrastructure; Security + Product/UX before materializing |
+| MAP_PROVIDER | recipient to declare (G07); not chosen |
+
+**Open / owner:**
+- **Protection values (Product/UX + Security).** Which values the person may choose for an activity, and whether protection may be turned off entirely. This is a tension between point 3 (editable) and "no residence exposure".
+- **Minimum visible route after protection (Product/UX + Security).**
+- **Inference from repeated shares (Security).** Residual risk when shares repeatedly start or end at the same place; Privacy Zones are the planned mitigation.
+- **Map provider (Engineering + Security, G07).** The provider and what its request reveals: it should carry no more than the share-safe area.
+- **Copy and legal text (G07).**
