+## Current amendment — PDR-1.10 / Growth Layer: distribution and retention as product capabilities, no social network · 2026-10-29
+
+Source/decisor for DR-124–132: the current direct [Founder request](../audits/growth-layer-2026-10-29/FOUNDER_REQUEST.md) of 2026-10-29. All nine are **DECIDED / CURRENT_PRODUCT_DECISION**. They select V1 capabilities, principles and priorities. They change no training rule, policy, Adaptive Engine or Coaching Core readiness, freeze, review, blocker or the human revalidation queue. Record, clause map and checks: [GRW record](../audits/growth-layer-2026-10-29/RECORD.md).
+
+| ID | Current decision / rationale | Scope, supersession, dependents |
+|---|---|---|
+| DR-124 | **Growth Layer thesis.** Vilumo is an Adaptive Hybrid Coach, deep in running + strength, **plus** light distribution and retention loops built into the product. The advantage stays the depth of hybrid coaching and the quality of adaptive decisions; the product does not try to match the breadth of fitness super-apps. **Principle: "Distribution is a product capability, but social networking is not required for V1 distribution."** The Growth Layer amplifies the coach and never competes with it for priority. Priority order: (1) a genuinely competent coach; (2) a mature experience; (3) the ability to demonstrate progress; (4) light retention and acquisition loops; (5) only then social/ecosystem expansion. | Bounded reformulation of C003: shareability, referral and web presence are deliberate acquisition and retention capabilities, not only possible side effects. Their effect stays a hypothesis (H002, H007): measured, never claimed. Consistent with L022 (not a super-app), C016/C022 (SOCIAL NETWORK ≠ EXTERNAL SHAREABILITY), C044 (Share optional) and C048 (anti-bloat). The Growth Layer is a capability set, not a pillar, tab, hub or destination; the new Figma decides its manifestation (DR-95: a capability does not require a surface). |
+| DR-125 | **Training/Safety authority prevails over Growth.** If Growth and Training conflict, Training/Safety wins. No growth mechanic (consistency, reward, celebration, share prompt, referral, notification or metric) may pressure the person to train, complete or compensate when the Adaptive Engine prescribes rest, recovery, load reduction, KEEP or HOLD. Honoring them is correct compliance (L008). Growth never edits, reinterprets or relaxes a sporting rule, policy, gate or clinical boundary. | Applies L008, L019, L020, L024 and C060 to the whole layer. Every Adaptive Engine / Coaching Core freeze, digest, review, blocker and readiness verdict, the open G01–G04, R6-POLICY-5 and the human revalidation queue stay as they are. No SSCTR review is needed, because no training rule changes. |
+| DR-126 | **Shareability as acquisition (capability 1).** Shareable outputs are a strategic growth capability, not visual finishing. V1 has concepts for: post-workout result; PR / milestone; weekly summary; evolution over time; a run with its route when the data exist; complete cards; transparent overlays for photos; formats for Stories and external sharing. Outputs are desirable, mature and coherent with the design system, never a generic AI-template look. Discreet branding is enough for discovery without killing the wish to share. Attribution is planned as a future chain, share generated → share completed → external visit → signup/install, with no infrastructure before a real consumer exists. | Extends C016–C018/C054, AR-15 (PA §7) and DR-81. Supersedes UXS SHR-12's V1 exclusion of milestone, streak and broad recap: milestone and recap are V1 concepts again and streak returns as consistency (DR-127); the new Figma decides how. Unchanged and binding: the PA §7 allowlist and SHR-06 exclusions; exact preview, explicit act and destination, no auto-post (C054). **Route and map: DR-133** (Map Share Privacy V1, PDR-1.11). Future attribution is first-party only: never imported likes, reach, audience or viewer identity (PDM I9, SHR-08). Any link or code inside an artifact is a visible, removable, opted-in field, never hidden metadata or an internal ID/token (SHR-06). Its privacy model is open (below). |
+| DR-127 | **Consistency, not naive streaks (capability 2).** Consistency gamification reflects training logic: adherence to the plan, consistent weeks, planned versus completed sessions, rest and recovery when prescribed, and sustainable consistency. **A naive daily streak in which planned rest days hurt the person is PROHIBITED.** Conceptual examples: "4 semanas consistentes", "8 de 9 sessões concluídas", "91% de aderência neste ciclo". Gamification never encourages training when the system recommends recovery. | Reformulates "personal streak" (C054, AR-15, SHR-01/07) as plan-adherence consistency; applies L008, L019, L020 and D007. What counts as completed, partial, a consistent week, tolerance and an honored adaptation is **G03** (open), so labels stay provisional until it closes. Unknown is neither failure nor success; no volume merit; no compensation pressure (CTN-06, HOJ-C15). Adherence % stays out of share artifacts (UXS §16.1, PA §7) until G03 and an allowlist decision. |
+| DR-128 | **History as proof of value (capability 3).** History becomes progressive longitudinal evidence, not only an activity archive: pace, times at distances, volume, loads, reps, frequency, adherence, PRs, running + strength evolution and comparison between cycles. It helps answer "Estou melhor do que quando comecei?" and, only when epistemically defensible, "O que mudou durante o período em que segui este treinamento?". No causal attribution to the Adaptive Engine when the data do not support it; no false-certainty language. | Consistent with RS §5 (observed ≠ estimate ≠ causality), C051, C060, DR-92 (history capability), PDM I12, RIL §6/§8 and STIL §8. Comparability G02/G03; estimates such as e1RM only with an approved model; efficacy claims G11. No new surface or tab is implied. |
+| DR-129 | **Minimal referral (capability 4).** The product architecture provides simple referral: an individual link/code, identification of the invite's origin, referral → signup, and a possible future reward (initial candidate: PRO days or a similar benefit). **Not now:** a sophisticated affiliate system, marketplace, wallet, revenue sharing or a complex financial structure. Build only when there is a real need. | **A product referral is not a Crew invite.** C041, PDM I4/I5/I8, RS §3, SHR-03 and CF F08 stay unchanged: no social link, relationship or graph visible in the product, no contact ingestion (§4), no notification about the other person and no shared data beyond the attribution itself. Pre-account attribution stays on the device until the account exists (DR-111). Purpose and retention G07; abuse and fraud (self-referral, fake accounts) G08 before any reward; reward, entitlement and terms G10. |
+| DR-130 | **Website / SEO pre-launch (capability 5).** After the product name is definitive, a web presence exists before or near launch: main landing; waitlist / early access; pages on hybrid training, running + strength training ("corrida + musculação"), reconciling running and the gym, and the adaptive coach. Competitor comparison pages may come later, when the launched product has enough evidence for responsible comparison. SEO is a long-term acquisition channel, not a giant content project before PMF. | The site is marketing presence, not a web product: V1 stays iOS-only (DR-120). Copy follows C060, L023 and G11: no efficacy, safety or sport-support claim beyond the evidence. Waitlist personal data: purpose, consent and legal text G07. Definitive name: Founder, open (DR-85 kept naming testable). Building the site is not authorized here. |
+| DR-131 | **Growth loops.** Acquisition loop: Adaptive Plan → Workout → Result → Progress → Shareable Artifact → External Discovery → New User; it needs no internal social graph. Retention loop: Plan → Execution → Adherence → Observable Progress → Increased Trust → Next Training Cycle; the product optimizes this cycle before seeking complex social mechanisms. | Growth readings of the C044 value loop (Decide → Prepare → Execute → Observe → Adapt → Share → Repeat): Share stays voluntary, and the individual loop works without it. "Adherence" includes honored rest and reduction (DR-125). Loops are concepts, not screens or step sequences. |
+| DR-132 | **North Star and product analytics (proposed).** Initial central metric: **Weekly Adapted Plan Completion Rate**, conceptually the share of eligible active users who sufficiently complete their prescribed/adapted weekly plan. Auxiliary metrics: Week-1 and Week-4 retention; planned versus completed sessions; consistent weeks; adherence; share creation rate; share completion rate; referral → signup; trial → paid; adaptation acceptance/completion where semantically valid. No metric without a consumer or an associated decision; no analytics infrastructure is created now. | The **operational definition is OPEN** under O001 (unit, window, denominator, context, missing data) and G03 (adherence criteria). It must follow Training Domain rules and is not invented here. Honored rest, reduction and HOLD count as completion, never as failure; raw activity, volume or daily streaks are never the target (L016, L020). Adaptation acceptance never rewards changing the plan: KEEP is a valid outcome (L024, C050, C060). Collection needs a G07 purpose, and nothing is collected before the account (DR-111). Owners: Data/Analytics with Product/UX; sporting semantics with the training authority (SSCTR within its bounded scope); the Founder decides value priority. |
+
+**Out of V1, unchanged by this decision:** Crew, social feed, social graph, clubs, chat, DMs, public ranking, events, complex community challenges, marketplace, the nutrition module, a full affiliate system and any internal social network. Crew/social stays **DEFERRED, NOT REJECTED** (C041, DR-76), to be re-evaluated after core validation.
+
+**Confirmed state:**
+
+| Item | State |
+|---|---|
+| GROWTH_LAYER | V1 capability set (five capabilities); not a pillar, tab or destination |
+| SOCIAL_NETWORK_REQUIRED_FOR_V1_DISTRIBUTION | NO |
+| TRAINING_SAFETY_OVER_GROWTH | YES |
+| NAIVE_DAILY_STREAK | PROHIBITED |
+| ROUTE_IN_SHARE | DR-133: Map, Route, Photo/Overlay or no route; first/last 200 m hidden by default |
+| SHARE_ATTRIBUTION | FUTURE; first-party; privacy model OPEN; no infrastructure now |
+| REFERRAL_V1 | MINIMAL (link/code, origin, referral → signup); reward OPEN (G10) |
+| WEBSITE_SEO | PRE_LAUNCH, after the definitive product name |
+| NORTH_STAR | WEEKLY_ADAPTED_PLAN_COMPLETION_RATE (concept); operational definition OPEN (O001, G03) |
+| CREW_SOCIAL_V1 | OUT — DEFERRED, NOT REJECTED |
+| ADAPTIVE_ENGINE_READINESS / FREEZES / BLOCKERS | UNCHANGED |
+
+**Open / owner:** definitive product name → Founder; adherence and consistency criteria → G03 (Product/UX with the training authority); North Star operational definition → O001 + G03 (Data/Analytics and Product/UX; Founder priority); attribution privacy model, the referral record and any link/code field in PA §7 → Product/UX + Security, with G07; referral abuse → G08; reward, trial and entitlement → G10; web and history claims → G11; experience manifestation → the new Figma under its own design mission; implementation of any part → a future Founder-authorized mission.
